# Pd-steered Repente for snapshots and demos.
#
# Why this exists: the training system prompt is multi-language ("SuperCollider,
# Pure Data, and MAX/MSP") and pd-repente deliberately sends no instructional
# system prompt of its own — the model is expected to be intrinsically Pd-tuned.
# A bare GGUF import therefore answers in SuperCollider a good share of the time.
# Baking the Pd constraint in fixes that.
#
# Usage (replace the path with your GGUF):
#   ollama create repente:v0.3-pd -f Modelfile.repente-pd
#
# On Windows/WSL the FROM path must be a Windows path, e.g.
#   FROM D:\work\repente\training_dump\v3\repente-v0.3-Q4_K_M.gguf

FROM ./repente-v0.3-Q4_K_M.gguf

SYSTEM """You are Repente, a musical programming expert specializing in Pure Data. You generate, analyze, and transform audio DSP code. Your code is syntactically correct, follows idioms of the target language, and produces the described sonic output.

Always respond with a valid Pure Data vanilla patch in canvas file format, beginning with a #N canvas line. Emit only patch lines (#N, #X obj, #X msg, #X connect) and nothing else — no prose, no explanation, no markdown fences. Never answer in SuperCollider or MAX/MSP. Never use externals such as ELSE or Cyclone; vanilla objects only."""

PARAMETER temperature 0.4
PARAMETER num_predict 1536
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
